Use this when the next transaction must wait for this one to finish on the bus. The invariant is that each acquired request is retired exactly once, and only one thread drives the pins. Template 08 is the concrete APB version.

**Interview answer.** "My driver polls with `try_next_item` on every clock, so the same thread that owns the pins can also hold them idle during reset. It copies the routing ID into the response and calls `item_done` once, after the bus completes."

Assumptions: `bus_req`, `bus_rsp`, the interface, and the `drive_one`/`drive_idle` helpers exist.

```systemverilog
// Inside uvm_driver #(bus_req, bus_rsp)
task run_phase(uvm_phase phase);
  bus_req req;
  bus_rsp rsp;
  drive_status_e status;

  forever begin
    @(vif.cb);
    if (vif.cb.rst_n !== 1'b1) begin
      drive_idle();
      continue;
    end

    // Polling lets the single pin owner handle reset while idle
    seq_item_port.try_next_item(req);
    if (req == null) begin
      drive_idle();
      continue;
    end

    rsp = bus_rsp::type_id::create("rsp");
    rsp.set_id_info(req);
    drive_one(req, rsp, status);
    rsp.status = status;
    drive_idle();
    seq_item_port.item_done(rsp);
  end
endtask
```

**Shorter blocking form.** `get_next_item(req); drive_one(req, rsp, status); item_done(rsp);` works only if some other mechanism handles reset while the driver is idle.

**APB outline (Q251).** Drive setup with `psel=1, penable=0`. On the next cycle drive access with `penable=1`. Hold address and control stable until `pready`. Sample read data and `pslverr` at completion, then go idle or start the next setup.

**Reset questions to raise.** Is reset synchronous or asynchronous? Does an in-flight item abort or retry? How does the scoreboard flush predictions that reset cancelled?

