Use this when you define the object passed between sequence, driver, monitor, and checker. The invariant is that only request fields are random, observed fields stay four-state so X is visible, and nested objects have an explicit copy rule.

**Interview answer.** "Request fields are `rand` and carry legality constraints. Response fields like `rdata` are `logic` and not random, so an X from the DUT stays visible. I register fields with the factory macros, and I compare only the fields that matter instead of calling the generic `compare()`."

```systemverilog
typedef enum {APB_OK, APB_ERR, APB_RESET} apb_status_e;
class apb_item extends uvm_sequence_item;
  rand bit [31:0] addr, wdata;
  rand bit write;
  rand bit [3:0] strb;
  logic [31:0] rdata;
  apb_status_e status;
  constraint legal_c {
    addr[1:0] == 0;
    addr inside {[32'h0:32'h3fc]};
    if (!write) strb == 0;
  }
  `uvm_object_utils_begin(apb_item)
    `uvm_field_int(addr, UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(wdata, UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(write, UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(strb, UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(rdata, UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_enum(apb_status_e, status, UVM_DEFAULT)
  `uvm_object_utils_end
  function new(string name = "apb_item");
    super.new(name);
    status = APB_RESET;
  endfunction
endclass
```

**Adaptations.** For error injection, add a negative-test subclass or turn off `legal_c` with `constraint_mode(0)` (Template 17). Record response latency as an observed field. Field macros keep the example short. In production code many teams write `do_copy` and `do_compare` by hand because the macros are slow and hide behavior.

### DMA descriptor adaptation (Q215)

The transaction is a copy command, not a bus beat. The descriptor gives source, destination, and length. The expected destination data is predicted from source memory, never randomized.

Example rules: contiguous copy, 32-bit addresses, 4-byte alignment, 4 to 4096 bytes, no overlap, no address wrap.

```systemverilog
class dma_item extends uvm_sequence_item;
  rand bit [31:0] src, dst;
  rand int unsigned nbytes;
  constraint legal_c {
    nbytes inside {[4:4096]};
    nbytes % 4 == 0;
    src[1:0] == 0; dst[1:0] == 0;
    (longint'(src) + nbytes) <= 64'h1_0000_0000;
    (longint'(dst) + nbytes) <= 64'h1_0000_0000;
    ((longint'(src) + nbytes) <= longint'(dst)) ||
    ((longint'(dst) + nbytes) <= longint'(src));
  }
  `uvm_object_utils_begin(dma_item)
    `uvm_field_int(src, UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(dst, UVM_DEFAULT)
    `uvm_field_int(nbytes, UVM_DEFAULT)
  `uvm_object_utils_end
  function new(string name = "dma_item"); super.new(name); endfunction
endclass
```

The `longint'` casts stop `src + nbytes` from wrapping at 32 bits. A programming sequence turns the descriptor into register writes and a start command. A memory responder supplies source bytes. The scoreboard snapshots the source when the copy starts, predicts the destination writes, and checks completion separately from register programming. Add channel, stride, or descriptor-chain fields only when the spec has them.

**Trace.** `src=0x100, dst=0x200, nbytes=16` predicts four word writes. With overlap forbidden, `dst=0x108` must fail randomization.

