Use this to implement Template 02 for the Template 05 contract. The invariant is that one thread owns the pins and each acquired request gets exactly one `item_done(response)`.

**Interview answer.** "On a falling edge I drive setup. On the next falling edge I raise PENABLE. Then I sample PREADY on each rising edge until it is high, capture PRDATA and PSLVERR, and return to idle. If reset appears, I abort, mark the response APB_RESET, and still call `item_done` once."

This driver leaves one idle cycle between transfers. It is simple, not maximum throughput.

```systemverilog
class apb_driver extends uvm_driver #(apb_item);
  `uvm_component_utils(apb_driver)
  virtual apb_if vif;
  function new(string name, uvm_component parent);
    super.new(name, parent);
  endfunction
  function void build_phase(uvm_phase phase);
    super.build_phase(phase);
    if (!uvm_config_db#(virtual apb_if)::get(this, "", "vif", vif))
      `uvm_fatal("NOVIF", "APB interface missing")
  endfunction
  task idle(); // Call only at a drv_cb event.
    vif.drv_cb.psel <= 0;
    vif.drv_cb.penable <= 0;
    vif.drv_cb.pwrite <= 0;
    vif.drv_cb.paddr <= 0;
    vif.drv_cb.pwdata <= 0;
    vif.drv_cb.pstrb <= 0;
    vif.drv_cb.pprot <= 0;
  endtask
  task transfer(apb_item q, apb_item r);
    // Entry is a falling-edge drv_cb event.
    r.status = APB_RESET;
    vif.drv_cb.psel <= 1;
    vif.drv_cb.penable <= 0;
    vif.drv_cb.paddr <= q.addr;
    vif.drv_cb.pwrite <= q.write;
    vif.drv_cb.pwdata <= q.wdata;
    vif.drv_cb.pstrb <= q.strb;
    vif.drv_cb.pprot <= 0;
    @(vif.mon_cb); // Rising edge samples setup, not completion.
    if (vif.mon_cb.presetn !== 1'b1) begin
      @(vif.drv_cb); idle(); return;
    end
    @(vif.drv_cb);
    if (vif.drv_cb.presetn !== 1'b1) begin
      idle(); return;
    end
    vif.drv_cb.penable <= 1;
    forever begin
      @(vif.mon_cb);
      if (vif.mon_cb.presetn !== 1'b1) break;
      if ($isunknown(vif.mon_cb.pready))
        `uvm_fatal("XREADY", "PREADY unknown during access")
      if (vif.mon_cb.pready === 1'b1) begin
        if ($isunknown(vif.mon_cb.pslverr))
          `uvm_fatal("XERR", "PSLVERR unknown at completion")
        r.rdata = vif.mon_cb.prdata;
        r.status = vif.mon_cb.pslverr ? APB_ERR : APB_OK;
        break;
      end
    end
    @(vif.drv_cb); idle();
  endtask
  task run_phase(uvm_phase phase);
    apb_item q, r;
    forever begin
      @(vif.drv_cb);
      idle();
      if (vif.drv_cb.presetn !== 1'b1) continue;
      q = null;
      seq_item_port.try_next_item(q);
      if (q == null) continue;
      r = apb_item::type_id::create("r");
      r.copy(q);
      r.set_id_info(q);
      transfer(q, r);
      seq_item_port.item_done(r);
    end
  endtask
endclass
```

**Trace.** Call the falling edges F0, F1, ... and the rising edges R1, R2, .... F0 drives setup. R1 samples setup. F1 drives access. R2 completes the transfer if PREADY is high. With two wait states, R2 and R3 see identical request signals and R4 completes. The next falling edge returns to idle, then the driver calls `item_done`. If reset is sampled at R3, the driver aborts and the monitor publishes no transfer for that access.

**When a transfer hangs.** The watchdog in Template 13 ends the test. Do not abandon an unfinished APB access and report it as a timeout completion. If the spec requires recovery, coordinate a reset and retire the cancelled work. If pins must clear asynchronously on reset, redesign pin ownership around reset rather than adding a second thread that writes the pins.

